0,Pardhan language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pardhan_language,"Pardhan (or Pradhan, IPA: [pɐrdʱaːn, prɐdʱaːn]) is a dialect of Gondi spoken by the Pardhan people, a community who are the traditional bards of the Gonds. Its speakers are found in areas where the Gonds live: southeastern Madhya Pradesh, far-eastern Maharashtra and northern Telangana.",Pardhan,Dravidian
1,Pardhan: A Glimpse Into The Lives Of Central India's Tribal ...,https://ebnw.net/art-craft/pardhan-a-glimpse-into-the-lives-of-central-indias-tribal-musicians/,"May 27, 2024 · The Pardhan are a unique subgroup of the Dravidian, tribal Gond people residing in central India. Known for their rich cultural heritage, the Pardhan have traditionally held the roles of singers and musicians, enlivening festivals and significant life ceremonies with their art.",Pardhan,Dravidian
